# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and personal state
#
# These are the entries that matter most. Everything below is either a
# credential or a record of real conversations, and git history is
# effectively permanent -- a secret committed once has to be treated as
# leaked even after a later commit deletes it.
#
# Kept deliberately in step with DENY_PATTERNS in package_release.py,
# which strips the same files from a shared build. If a new one is added
# there, add it here too.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
assistant/.model_api_key
assistant/.audit_hmac_key
assistant/.dev_passcode
assistant/.super_dev_passcode
assistant/.tdeck_ble_pin
assistant/.spotify_token
# The read-only agent interface's bearer token. Belongs to one running
# installation, and committing it would hand every clone a live credential.
assistant/.agent_token
assistant/.activity_consent.json
assistant/.safety_acknowledgement.json
# Owner-supplied cloud API keys for the opt-in escalation bridge. These are
# billing credentials for external accounts -- strictly worse to leak than
# any local token.
assistant/.anthropic_api_key
assistant/.openai_api_key
*.env
*secrets*

# Real conversations, and the memories extracted from them.
assistant/memory/conversation_history.txt
assistant/memory/activity_log.jsonl
assistant/memory/wifi_sensing_status.json
assistant/memory/memories.json
assistant/memory/change_plans/
assistant/memory/plan_*.txt
# Session timings. No text, but when the operator sits down, how long they
# stay, and how long they pause is behavioural data about a person. It went
# unlisted here for as long as nothing wrote it.
assistant/memory/session_rhythm.json

# Offline knowledge imported by the operator and its derived index. The
# built-in action cards are source; user manuals and their vectors are private
# installation data and can be very large.
assistant/knowledge/library.sqlite3*
assistant/knowledge/user_library/*
!assistant/knowledge/user_library/.gitkeep

# The absence of this file is what marks a fresh install, so it must
# never be tracked -- committing it would deny every clone its first-run
# walkthrough.
assistant/.tutorial_state.json

# The name the director chose for itself. Same reasoning: it belongs to a
# running install, not to the source tree. Committing one would hand every
# clone a name it did not choose, which is the one thing the ceremony exists
# to avoid.
assistant/memory/chosen_name.json


# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated runtime state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
assistant/logs/
assistant/backups/
assistant/cache/
*.bak
*.backup
dump/
# Legacy root-level runtime placeholders are not source files.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash. Written bare, these match a directory of
# that name at ANY depth, so `memory/` silently swallowed the whole of
# assistant/memory/ -- every source module in it was invisible to git and
# survived only because files already tracked stay tracked. A new module
# added there committed clean and simply did not exist for anyone else.
# The specific private files under assistant/memory/ are listed above.
/memory/
# Obsolete captured wiring logs; they are neither source nor runtime state.
/wirelog/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Models and large binaries
#
# Multi-gigabyte weights do not belong in git. They are downloadable,
# and committing one makes every future clone pay for it forever.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
models/*.gguf
# One level down too: the embedding model lives in models/embedding/, and
# a bare models/*.gguf only matches the top level.
models/**/*.gguf
# Interrupted or quarantined downloads keep a suffix after .gguf, so the
# pattern above does not catch them. A 22 MB partial is still 22 MB.
models/**/*.gguf.*
models/voice/cache/
models/voice/**/*.onnx
models/voice/**/*.onnx.json


# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendored third-party trees
#
# Each of these carries its own .git directory. Tracked naively they
# become empty gitlinks that clone into nothing -- worse than absent,
# because the code looks present when it is not. They are upstream
# projects, re-clonable on demand.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
llama.cpp/
firmware/
searxng/

# An 83MB ffmpeg binary pip pulled in for the voice analysis scripts.
# Downloadable, platform-specific, and would otherwise be 96% of the
# repository by size.
voice_training/.analysis_tools/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
#
# dist/ is the shareable package: several gigabytes, rebuilt in full by
# package_release.py from the sources that ARE tracked here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
dist/
build/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Media
#
# The music library is someone else's copyright, and is excluded from
# shared builds for the same reason. Voice training samples are large
# generated renders, reproducible from the scripts that are kept.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
assistant/music/*
!assistant/music/.gitkeep
voice_training/samples*/
*.mp3
*.wav

# Generated icon frames and the shortcut variants built from them. Both
# come from glitch_icon.py --setup, and the .lnk files embed absolute
# paths from this machine.
icon_anim/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The workshop
#
# Everything in here is written by the goal engine, unprompted. It is
# genuinely interesting to read, but it is this machine's output rather
# than the project's source -- and it changes on its own, which would
# make every git status noisy. The folder itself is kept so a fresh
# clone has somewhere to work.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
workshop/*
!workshop/.gitkeep


# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Personal launchers
#
# Wrappers that set environment overrides for one machine -- a maintainer
# who wants voice mode on at startup, say, which Beta 6 deliberately
# turned off for everyone else. Keeping them out of the tree means a
# personal preference can never quietly become the shipped default.
#
# The packager selects root launchers from an explicit list rather than a
# glob, so these are excluded from a build regardless of this entry. The
# two guards are independent on purpose.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
*.local.bat

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and tool-local settings
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw research-evidence artifacts
#
# The Research C collectors freeze two kinds of file. Most of what they
# write is already privacy-safe by construction and is meant to be
# published -- READMEs, reanalyses, gradings, manifests, summaries, the
# independent audit. These four are not.
#
# preflight_prompts.json and *_stable_messages.json hold the *exact*
# runtime system prompt as it was sent, which carries installation-local
# chosen-name state; the rate spec and rows carry absolute host paths in
# their binding records. A sanitized public derivative of each is what
# gets committed instead, alongside a SHA-256 commitment to the original
# so the private file stays verifiable without being published.
#
# Listed as exact paths rather than a glob over the experiment folders,
# because the default for evidence is to publish it and a broad rule here
# would quietly swallow the parts that should be shared.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
handoffs/researchc_experiments_2026-07-30/preflight_prompts.json
handoffs/researchc_experiments_2026-07-30/rate_distortion/rate_distortion_stable_messages.json
handoffs/researchc_experiments_2026-07-30/rate_distortion/rate_distortion_spec.json
handoffs/researchc_experiments_2026-07-30/rate_distortion/rate_distortion_rows.jsonl

# Release staging, rebuilt by tools; never committed.
SABLERESEARCHA/
